context_info = ()
for d in context:
    prompt = "Here is a document:\nBEGIN_DOCUMENT\n" + d + "\nEND_DOCUMENT\n\nYour task is to extract only what this document itself states (no outside knowledge). We are looking for information relevant to this query:\n\nIn a specific European club competition season prior to 2023, three players had identical statistics for top scorers, with one player being from a rival team. During this season, a particular club recorded: highest match attendance in the season on a Wednesday, played a total of 13 matches, had the most assists in the season, and committed a total of 19 fouls resulting in cards. The club won the league. For that club, who scored the first goal for their third game in the group stage?\n\nFrom the document, extract any of the following if present (only if explicitly stated in the document):\n- Competition and season (e.g., UEFA Champions League 2014–15).\n- The list of top scorers and whether three players were joint top-scorers (identical goals), including if one is from a rival team of the title-winning club.\n- A club that season with all/some of these stats: highest match attendance on a Wednesday; total of 13 matches played; most assists; 19 fouls resulting in cards; and that the club won the competition.\n- For that club, list group stage Matchday 1 to Matchday 6 opponents and results if available, and specifically identify for Matchday 3: opponent, date, scoreline, and who scored the club’s first goal (and minute if available).\n\nOutput exactly in this format (include only items the document explicitly supports; otherwise omit the field):\nSeason_and_Competition: <...>\nClub: <...>\nTop_Scorers: <...>\nHighest_Attendance_Wednesday: <...>\nMatches_Played_Total: <...>\nMost_Assists_Team: <...>\nCards_From_Fouls_Total: <...>\nWon_Title: <...>\nGroup_Matches: <list or description>\nThird_Match_First_Scorer: <player name, minute if given>\nEvidence: \"<verbatim quotes that support the above>\"\nIf the document has none of this, write: No relevant info."
    result = llm_query(prompt)
    context_info = context_info + (result,)

synthesis_prompt = "You are given extractions from multiple documents. Use ONLY these extractions (do not use outside knowledge). Identify the single club and season that match all of the user's constraints, then answer the final question.\n\nDocuments:\n" + "\n\n---\n\n".join(context_info) + "\n\nUser question to answer concisely: In that season, for the club that fits all constraints and won the league, who scored the first goal for their third game in the group stage? Reply with ONLY the player's full name. If the documents do not provide enough information to uniquely determine the answer, reply exactly: Insufficient information."
final_answer = llm_query(synthesis_prompt)
return_result(final_answer)